cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use witness-cpp in academic or engineering work, please cite it as below."
title: "witness-cpp: exception-free property-testing ladder for C++"
abstract: >-
  Header-only C++17 property-testing library. Implements an
  iterative-deepening ladder over deterministically seeded random
  trials, with generators, shrinkers, assume/classify, and a
  reproducer seed printed on every falsified property. Uses no
  exceptions anywhere in its own code and its CI proves this by
  building the test binary with -fno-exceptions -fno-rtti, so it can
  be embedded in codebases that ship with exceptions disabled
  (Godot, LLVM, embedded).
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-11"
repository-code: "https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/witness-cpp"
keywords:
  - property-testing
  - random-testing
  - shrinking
  - cpp17
  - exception-free
  - header-only
  - doctest
references:
  - type: software
    title: "plausible-witness-dag"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    abstract: >-
      Lean/Lake library that layers an iterative-deepening ladder and
      deterministic readback over Plausible. The Level struct here
      (walk_steps, fin_bound, num_inst) mirrors its rungs and the
      DEFAULT_LADDER values here match the Lean-side defaults verbatim.
      witness-cpp is a fresh C++ implementation of the ladder shape,
      not a port of any Lean code.
    repository-code: "https://github.com/fire/plausible-witness-dag"
  - type: software
    title: "Plausible"
    abstract: >-
      Lean-community property-testing library used underneath
      plausible-witness-dag. The num_inst semantics and the
      FOUND / PROVABLY_NONE / BUDGET_HIT outcome triple in
      witness::Outcome reproduce Plausible's Testable.checkIO
      result classification.
    repository-code: "https://github.com/leanprover-community/plausible"
    license: Apache-2.0
  - type: software
    title: "doctest"
    authors:
      - family-names: Kirilov
        given-names: Viktor
    abstract: >-
      Single-header C++ test framework used by witness-cpp's own test
      suite and by the optional witness/doctest.h bindings. Chosen for
      being header-only and for defining DOCTEST_CONFIG_NO_EXCEPTIONS
      variants so the test binary can build under -fno-exceptions.
    repository-code: "https://github.com/doctest/doctest"
    license: MIT
